From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH perf 003] panvk/csf: raise the kbase CS ring buffer to 256KB

The kbase CSF queue used a 64KB ring, the panthor default. On this driver
the whole command stream of a submission is written into that ring before
the kick, so a tiled render pass of ~1.5 frames fills it and
kbase_subqueue_reserve_ring() blocks on the GPU seqno in the middle of
building the next submission, stalling the CPU thread.

256KB keeps the CPU well ahead of the GPU. The size is kept deliberately
modest: the kernel rejects a queue size it does not support at
CS_QUEUE_REGISTER time (which would fail queue creation), and the accepted
maximum is not exposed to userspace. If a kernel refuses 256KB, revert this
patch rather than growing the ring further.

Purpose: remove mid-submit CPU stalls when the GPU falls behind.
Tested GPU: build only, not yet run on device.
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21.
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f).
Dependencies: perf/001 (same file).
Validation test: TBD, on-device render + queue bind check in logcat
("Failed to bind a kbase CS queue" must not appear).

Generated-by: LLM

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c
index 5c9938f..0732b9d 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c
@@ -54,7 +54,14 @@
  * for completion; ordinary queue submission remains asynchronous.
  */
 
-#define KBASE_RINGBUF_SIZE     (64 * 1024)
+/* 64KB (the panthor default) is only ~1.5 frames of command stream on a
+ * tiled render pass: kbase_subqueue_reserve_ring() then has to block on the
+ * GPU seqno in the middle of building a submission. 256KB leaves enough
+ * slack to keep the CPU ahead. Kept deliberately modest: the kernel rejects
+ * a queue size it does not support at CS_QUEUE_REGISTER time, which would
+ * fail queue creation, and the accepted maximum is not exposed to
+ * userspace. */
+#define KBASE_RINGBUF_SIZE     (256 * 1024)
 /* Worst-case size of one ring entry, in bytes. Diagnostic breadcrumbs add a
  * few extra LS stores, so keep this conservatively above the normal panthor
  * kernel ring slot size. */
